  "body": "Reported by a Sodick wire EDM owner (@spikeypineapple) on #617, 2026-11-16:\n\n> I can say for sure this won't work. It might work on older machines, but it won't run on a ln1/ln2/ln3 control (anything made in the last 20 years).\n\n**What the LN controls expect** (his report): the condition codes follow the passes:\n- `C000` - entering the cut (a stable condition, so the wire does not break)\n- `C001` - rough cut\n- `C002` - sizing / second cut\n- `C903` and up - polishing passes\n\n**What the post does now** (`assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps`, main 1ae4d061f):\n- writes ONE condition word per operation, the operation's own condition id (`C` + three digits), line 296;\n- refuses a condition change between passes (skims), line 186, and sends skims to `wire-iso` instead;\n- writes no entry condition before the cut.\n\nSo a normal 1- or 2-pass part on a current Sodick cannot be posted as the control expects. Nothing gouges, and the workaround (`wire-iso`, or one operation per pass) exists, so P3 by the AGENTS.md table.\n\n**Scope** (his suggestion): 2 passes first - entry `C000`, rough `C001`, sizing `C002`. Polishing (`C903+`) later.\n\n**Open questions for the reporter** (asked on #617): where in the program each C word goes (on the threading/entry move, at each pass start); whether `C000` is used for every start hole; an example program from an LN control (his earlier AQ600L example on #617 shows a condition table in the header).\n\nClean-room: no CAM vendor's Sodick post or output is used; only the owner's own description and public Sodick manuals.\n\nDone means: the Sodick post writes the C000/C001/C002 structure for a 1- and 2-pass Wire Contour, pinned by golden programs, and the owner confirms on an LN control (or the open questions are answered on this issue).\n\nPart of #617. Related: #1500 (LN program format), #2130.\n",
